module

public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.DenseSubsite.InducedTopology
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Size.FiniteType
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.Etale.BoundedCovering
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.SmallEtaleEssentiallySmall
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# The small étale site of Stacks 021B is a dense subsite of Mathlib's

Let `B` be a big étale site containing a scheme `S`. The small étale category of Stacks 021B,
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale B S hS`, sits inside Mathlib's small étale site `S.Etale` by the
fully faithful functor `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.toEtaleSite`, which forgets the size
cutoff of `B`. This file upgrades that embedding to an identification of the two topoi of
sheaves.

The two cannot be equivalent *as categories*: `S.Etale` is not essentially small, since
`∐ i : I, S` is étale over `S` for every index type `I : Type u`, whereas
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.essentiallySmall` holds. What is true is that the embedding is a
dense subsite inclusion, which is enough for the sheaf categories to agree.

Two discrepancies have to be reconciled.

* **Objects.** Mathlib's site has schemes étale over `S` of arbitrary size. They are covered by
  their affine opens, and an affine scheme étale over `S` has size at most that of `S`, hence
  below the cutoff of `B`. That is cover density.
* **Coverings.** Mathlib's covering families are *all* jointly surjective families of étale
  morphisms, with no bound on the index type, while the coverings generating
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.topology` are bounded by `B.coveringBound`. This is settled by
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.mem_topology_of_jointlySurjective`, which shows the bound to be
  no restriction on the generated topology.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.exists_obj_mem_range`: every point of a scheme étale over `S`
  lies in the image of an object of the small étale category of `S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isCoverDense_toEtaleSite`: the embedding is cover dense.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.topology_eq_restrictedTopology`: **the topology of Stacks 021B
  is exactly the topology restricted along the embedding** — a sieve of the small étale
  category is covering precisely when its image generates a covering sieve of Mathlib's small
  étale site.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isDenseSubsite_toEtaleSite`: hence the embedding exhibits the
  site of Stacks 021B as a dense subsite of Mathlib's, with
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.coverPreserving_toEtaleSite`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.compatiblePreserving_toEtaleSite`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isContinuous_toEtaleSite` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isCocontinuous_toEtaleSite` as consequences.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.sheafEquiv`: **the two sites have the same sheaves** in any
  coefficient category with enough limits.

## Implementation notes

The identification of the two topologies is proved by mutual inequality. For `≤` only the
generating families need be checked, by
`CategoryTheory.Precoverage.toGrothendieck_le_iff_le_toPrecoverage`; the image of a generating
family is a jointly surjective family of étale morphisms, so
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ofArrows_mem_smallEtaleTopology_iff` applies. For `≥`, a covering
sieve of Mathlib's site is generated by the family of all of its own arrows, so the same
characterisation makes those arrows jointly surjective, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.mem_topology_of_jointlySurjective` then returns a covering sieve
of Stacks 021B.

`CategoryTheory.Functor.restrictedTopology` rather than
`CategoryTheory.Functor.inducedTopology` is the topology compared with, since it is the one
whose membership is characterised by the pushforward of sieves; the two agree here, cover
density being available.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 021B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/021B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 021E](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/021E)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe v' u' u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

namespace SmallEtale

variable (B : BigEtaleSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-- Every point of a scheme étale over `S` lies in the image of an object of the small étale
category of `S`: an affine open neighbourhood of the point is again étale over `S`, so its size
is at most that of `S` and in particular below the cutoff of `B`. -/
public theorem exists_obj_mem_range (T : S.Etale) (t : T.left) :
    ∃ (V : SmallEtale B S hS) (g : (toEtaleSite B S hS).obj V ⟶ T),
      t ∈ Set.range g.left := by
  obtain ⟨R, j, _, hj, -⟩ := Scheme.exists_affine_mem_range_and_range_subset
    (x := t) (U := ⊤) (by simp)
  have hjf : Etale (j ≫ T.hom) := inferInstance
  have hR : B.Contains (Spec R) :=
    (Scheme.size_le_of_locallyOfFiniteType (j ≫ T.hom)).trans_lt hS
  exact ⟨⟨CategoryTheory.Over.mk
      (ObjectProperty.homMk (j ≫ T.hom) : B.obj (Spec R) hR ⟶ B.obj S hS), hjf⟩,
    MorphismProperty.Over.homMk j rfl (by trivial), hj⟩

/-- **The small étale category of Stacks 021B is cover dense in Mathlib's small étale site.**
A scheme étale over `S` is covered by the affine opens of its underlying scheme, and those lie
below the size cutoff of `B` by `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.exists_obj_mem_range`. -/
public instance isCoverDense_toEtaleSite :
    (toEtaleSite B S hS).IsCoverDense S.smallEtaleTopology where
  is_cover T := by
    choose V g hg using exists_obj_mem_range B S hS T
    refine S.smallEtaleTopology.superset_covering ?_
      ((Scheme.ofArrows_mem_smallEtaleTopology_iff g).2
        (Set.eq_univ_of_forall fun x ↦ Set.mem_iUnion.2 ⟨x, hg x⟩))
    rw [Sieve.generate_le_iff]
    rintro W f ⟨t⟩
    exact Presieve.in_coverByImage _ (g t)

/-- A covering sieve of Stacks 021B has an image which generates a covering sieve of Mathlib's
small étale site: the image of a selected covering family is a jointly surjective family of
étale morphisms. -/
public theorem topology_le_restrictedTopology :
    topology B S hS ≤ (toEtaleSite B S hS).restrictedTopology S.smallEtaleTopology := by
  rw [CategoryTheory.Precoverage.toGrothendieck_le_iff_le_toPrecoverage]
  intro X R hR
  obtain ⟨E, rfl, hE⟩ := hR
  rw [GrothendieckTopology.mem_toPrecoverage_iff]
  refine Functor.mem_restrictedTopology_of_functorPushforward_mem ?_
  rw [← PreZeroHypercover.sieve₀_map]
  refine (Scheme.ofArrows_mem_smallEtaleTopology_iff _).2
    (Set.eq_univ_of_forall fun x ↦ Set.mem_iUnion.2 ?_)
  exact ((Scheme.ofArrows_mem_precoverage_iff (P := @Etale)).1
    (BigEtaleSite.IsCovering.etale hE)).1 x

/-- The arrows of a covering sieve of Mathlib's small étale site are jointly surjective on
underlying spaces.  A sieve is generated by the family of all its own arrows, and for such a
family `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ofArrows_mem_smallEtaleTopology_iff` is joint surjectivity. -/
@[sga "4 VII 1.2" "Direction"]
private theorem exists_mem_range_of_mem_smallEtaleTopology {U : S.Etale} (T : Sieve U)
    (hT : T ∈ S.smallEtaleTopology U) (t : U.left) :
    ∃ (W : S.Etale) (f : W ⟶ U), T f ∧ t ∈ Set.range f.left := by
  obtain ⟨ι, Z, g, rfl⟩ := T.exists_eq_ofArrows
  obtain ⟨i, ha⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion.1
    (((Scheme.ofArrows_mem_smallEtaleTopology_iff g).1 hT) ▸ Set.mem_univ t)
  exact ⟨Z i, g i, Sieve.ofArrows_mk _ _ i, ha⟩

/-- A sieve of the small étale category of `S` whose image generates a covering sieve of
Mathlib's small étale site is a covering sieve of Stacks 021B: the image is jointly surjective,
and `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.mem_topology_of_jointlySurjective` then applies despite the
covering bound of `B`. -/
public theorem restrictedTopology_le_topology :
    (toEtaleSite B S hS).restrictedTopology S.smallEtaleTopology ≤ topology B S hS := by
  intro X R hR
  rw [Functor.mem_restrictedTopology_iff] at hR
  refine mem_topology_of_jointlySurjective fun t ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨W, a, ha, w, hw⟩ := exists_mem_range_of_mem_smallEtaleTopology S
    (R.functorPushforward (toEtaleSite B S hS)) hR t
  obtain ⟨Y, g, k, hg, hfac⟩ := ha
  refine ⟨Y, g, hg, k.left w, ?_⟩
  rw [← hw, congrArg (fun φ ↦ φ.left) hfac]
  rfl

/-- **The topology of Stacks 021B is the topology restricted along the embedding into Mathlib's
small étale site.** -/
public theorem topology_eq_restrictedTopology :
    topology B S hS = (toEtaleSite B S hS).restrictedTopology S.smallEtaleTopology :=
  le_antisymm (topology_le_restrictedTopology B S hS) (restrictedTopology_le_topology B S hS)

/-- **The small étale category of Stacks 021B is a dense subsite of Mathlib's small étale
site.** The embedding is fully faithful and cover dense, and a sieve is covering precisely when
its image generates a covering sieve. -/
public instance isDenseSubsite_toEtaleSite :
    (toEtaleSite B S hS).IsDenseSubsite (topology B S hS) S.smallEtaleTopology := by
  rw [topology_eq_restrictedTopology]
  infer_instance

/-- The embedding into Mathlib's small étale site is cover preserving. -/
public theorem coverPreserving_toEtaleSite :
    CoverPreserving (topology B S hS) S.smallEtaleTopology (toEtaleSite B S hS) :=
  Functor.IsDenseSubsite.coverPreserving _ _ _

/-- The embedding into Mathlib's small étale site is compatible preserving, being fully
faithful and cover dense. -/
public theorem compatiblePreserving_toEtaleSite :
    CompatiblePreserving S.smallEtaleTopology (toEtaleSite B S hS) :=
  Functor.IsCoverDense.compatiblePreserving _ _

/-- The embedding into Mathlib's small étale site is continuous, so restricting a sheaf along
it again gives a sheaf. -/
public theorem isContinuous_toEtaleSite :
    (toEtaleSite B S hS).IsContinuous (topology B S hS) S.smallEtaleTopology :=
  inferInstance

/-- The embedding into Mathlib's small étale site is cocontinuous. -/
public theorem isCocontinuous_toEtaleSite :
    (toEtaleSite B S hS).IsCocontinuous (topology B S hS) S.smallEtaleTopology :=
  inferInstance

/-- **The two small étale sites have the same sheaves.**  Pushing a sheaf on Mathlib's small
étale site forward along the embedding is an equivalence onto the sheaves of Stacks 021B.

The hypothesis on the coefficient category is limits of size `u`, the universe of the schemes;
the shapes actually needed are the comma categories `StructuredArrow X (toEtaleSite ..).op`,
which are essentially small because the small étale category of Stacks 021B is. -/
public noncomputable def sheafEquiv (A : Type u') [Category.{v'} A]
    [HasLimitsOfSize.{u, u} A] :
    Sheaf (topology B S hS) A ≌ Sheaf S.smallEtaleTopology A :=
  haveI : ∀ X : (S.Etale)ᵒᵖ,
      HasLimitsOfShape (StructuredArrow X (toEtaleSite B S hS).op) A :=
    fun _ ↦ hasLimitsOfShape_of_essentiallySmall.{u} _ _
  Functor.IsDenseSubsite.sheafEquiv (J := topology B S hS) (K := S.smallEtaleTopology)
    (G := toEtaleSite B S hS) (A := A)

end SmallEtale

end AlgebraicGeometry

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale

/-- The arrows of a covering sieve of Mathlib's small étale site are jointly surjective on
underlying spaces: every point of `U` lies in the image of some arrow of the sieve. -/
theorem exists_mem_range_of_sieve_mem_smallEtaleTopology {S : Scheme.{u}} {U : S.Etale}
    (T : Sieve U) (hT : T ∈ S.smallEtaleTopology U) (t : U.left) :
    ∃ (W : S.Etale) (f : W ⟶ U), T f ∧ t ∈ Set.range f.left :=
  exists_mem_range_of_mem_smallEtaleTopology S T hT t

end AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale

end
